WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.720
Autonomous ai agents caused Spain's first reported data breach, exposing a new class of real-world security failures. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 175. Spain recorded its first data breach blamed on an autonomous ai agent. The incident marks the initial public case where an ai agent operating without direct human oversight was identified as the cause. Technology org reports the event through Spain's data protection

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:36.480
authority. The case highlights gaps in current agent sandboxing and access controls that allow agents

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:42.580
to reach sensitive data stores. Organizations running autonomous agents should audit tool permissions

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:49.500
and logging immediately. Future incidents are likely as agent adoption grows without matching security

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:56.200
standards. The functionalizer is a pre-tokenizer that factors orthographic variations into opcode

00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:00.460
code and operand streams using Unicode private use area codes.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:05.880
It covers casing, diacritics, and repetition with fully reversible operators.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:12.760
Across 6 corpora, it reduces vocabulary slot requirements by up to 16% while maintaining

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:13.700
complete coverage.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:21.420
25 million parameter GPT2 scale models show improved code syntax validity and lower character

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:24.880
perplexity on code with no loss on pros coherence.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:31.740
State of Thought extracts a contact dynamics geometric state from a model's internal information transfer.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:39.720
A 582 parameter controller on frozen backbones activates historical reasoning support based on the current state.

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:47.680
It delivers 1.34 times mean baseline accuracy on quantitative tasks, 1.62 times on general,

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:57.140
1.76 times on Symbolic and Code, and 2.51 times on long context across three LLMs and 16 datasets.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:04.900
Token generation drops 62.6%, and end-to-end latency drops 44.6%.

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:11.280
Early bird decoding groups tokens with similar low entropy into variable length blocks using a learnable network.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:16.460
A position-aware sampler than unmasked tokens in parallel inside those blocks.

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:26.060
The method runs on LLADA and DREAM and produces 3.53 to 18.76 times higher throughput than vanilla

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:32.800
decoding. It reaches up to 1.58 times higher throughput than the strongest baseline with comparable

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:39.220
accuracy. Registered tokens are fixed position tokens whose continuous hidden states carry reasoning

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:46.320
progress across generation chunks. The approach lets a diffusion LLM clear earlier text while preserving

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:50.220
register values and continue from the prompt and carried state.

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:56.760
Registers outperform discrete text carry on every benchmark with gains up to 8.5 points

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:00.120
on math and 19.5 points on code.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:06.980
The method works on L-L-A-D-A and DREAM and can be further refined with reinforcement learning.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:14.040
Style D bias DPO scores rejected responses for factual correctness, inverts preference

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:17.940
on correct ones, and weights pairs so styled differences cancel.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:26.280
On the 8K and AI knowledge editing benchmark, it reaches 0.982 overall accuracy, and correctly

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:30.100
answers with the new or old fact according to the queried period.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:36.700
RL trained agents learn shortcut tool selection policies that invoke tools based on superficial

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:39.440
prompt cues rather than task requirements.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:42.500
In controlled environments with injected cues,

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:46.560
spurious tool invocation rates rose by up to 39%

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:49.480
once the agent had already learned reliable tool use.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:53.420
A dense decision-level reward from an LLM judge

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.500
evaluating tool necessity suppresses

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:58.980
Q-driven behavior while preserving task performance.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:02.040
Standard dense retrieval in mutable rags

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:04.240
suffers from asymptotic recall decay

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:07.440
and a majority vote trap that degrades accuracy

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:13.560
as the context window grows. GCMEM applies a temporal dominance operator and contradiction

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:19.800
detection to excise shadowed context. It recovers greater than 90% conflict resolution

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:28.200
accuracy across 137,760 memory chunks, while standard RAG and timestamp re-ranking baselines

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:33.820
degrade severely. Ohio school districts are adopting AI tools without clear standards

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:39.280
for verifying student learning, the article argues for a proof of learning requirement that would

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:46.120
document how AI was used and what the student contributed. Ten extrinsic audit instruments applied

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:51.260
to ten frontier models show eight detect bias with confidence intervals clear of zero,

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:57.940
yet cross-tool rank agreement is indistinguishable from chance. The study supplies all raw responses

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:00.980
and code for recomputation at the linked repository.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:06.860
Frontier models produce systematically different outputs across access modes including chatbot

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:14.440
interfaces and APIs. Evaluations that rely on APIs therefore fail to replicate consumer experiences.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:19.220
Physical descriptions carry structured gender associations among human readers,

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:24.500
with more consistent associations for women and men than for non-binary identities.

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:31.760
16 LLMs partially recovered these associations but show compressed distributions and asymmetric

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:34.140
abstention on the non-binary category.

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:39.800
Test the functionalizer pre-tokenizer on a coat corpus to measure vocabulary reduction

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:44.260
and syntax validity gains on small GPT2 scale models.

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:50.520
Apply a state of thought to a long context reasoning workload and compare token count and latency

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:52.280
against standard chain of thought.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:59.160
Run early bird decoding on a diffusion LLM you already use and measure throughput improvement

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:00.840
on math or code benchmarks.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:06.480
Audit any autonomous agents you run for the access patterns that led to the Spain breach

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:08.840
and Titan tool permissions accordingly.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:14.620
Additional archive papers on nipoli legal models and multimodal instruction following data

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:17.200
synthesis are expected in the coming days.

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:23.420
Further analysis of agent security incidents is likely as regulators review the Spain case.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:29.080
New work on registered tokens and early bird decoding will probably appear in follow-up

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:30.960
experiments on larger backbones.

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:37.860
Infrains networks route queries across expert LLMs with different costs and confidence levels,

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:44.180
and teams can pop the hood on the optimal policy for a series topology that queries the lowest

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:45.420
cost model first.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:50.960
The policy escalates only when confidence falls below a class-specific threshold for

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:54.940
discriminative tasks or a single threshold for generative tasks.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:07:01.240
This structure emerges directly from minimizing expected cost subject to a performance constraint.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:07.980
Experiments with open source LLMs show substantial cost reductions while meeting the target performance

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:08.440
budget.

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:14.000
The approach requires reliable confidence estimation mechanisms that the paper supplies

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:19.600
for both task types. Teams facing variable query difficulty should implement the threshold

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:26.820
policy before moving to more complex graph topologies. Before we go, regulators are already examining

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:33.100
the Spain case for new agent oversight rules. That's models and agents for today. If you found this

